This is a plain text file pretending to be a JPEG image by its file
extension alone. It contains no actual image data whatsoever -- no JPEG
file signature, no pixel data, nothing a real image decoder could parse.

This file exists specifically to test that your validation logic checks
the real file signature (the actual bytes at the start of the file)
rather than trusting the .jpg extension or a client-declared MIME type,
both of which are trivial for anyone to fake.

If your app correctly rejects this file, that confirms the security-
conscious validation approach implemented in Stage C-D is working as
intended.
